From 9e00c2ecd7cee81b049bccacf86db76d8c2d119c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 16:48:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/53] B70-IP-K4b/K5: scratch sized at impl init; FA-bf16
 prefill over fp8 KV

K4b: the one-layer bf16 prefill scratch is sized to max_model_len captured
in the attention impl __init__ (the vLLM config is not current at forward;
the old lookup fell back to 131072 and split >139K prompts onto Triton).
Measured: QFN dense int8 KV boots with 82 x 3264 blocks (full 262,144).

K5: on XPU the FA kernel fp8-KV path is ~2.2x slower than its bf16 path for
prefill chunks (B70 hs=256: 63.1 vs 28.9 ms, 4096 q over 32K). FLASH_ATTN
with fp8 KV now dequantizes the referenced blocks into the same bf16 scratch
and runs FA bf16 for batches with max q > B70_PTH_FA_MIN_Q; decode and
spec-verify stay on the fp8 kernel and graphs. Fires in QFN dense warmup
(log line seen); gates pending a full boot. B70_PTH_FA_PREFILL=0 disables.
